{
  "info": {
    "name": "OAN Messaging Service (contract 3.2.0)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "SMS (8028) and Telegram delivery for OAN services. Contract: docs/openapi.yaml (3.2.0).\n\nSetup: import an environment from docs/postman, paste the caller token into `callerToken` (and a statistics-reader token into `statsToken` for Charts). Tokens are issued by the OAN operator (`python -m oan_messaging.runtime issue-credential`); keep them as secret values, never commit or share them.\n\nEvery POST needs an `Idempotency-Key` (8 to 128 of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ : -). The collection makes a new one per request; a real caller uses one stable key per intended message and reuses it on every retry. 202 = new, 200 = identical replay (same id), 409 = same key with a different body.\n\nRules: one recipient per message (Ethiopian mobile: 09/07 series, 2519..., +2519...). An `otp` must carry `expires_at` and fit one SMS part (160 GSM-7 or 70 characters if any Amharic/Unicode). Other texts may use up to 3 parts (459 GSM-7 / 201 Unicode). 202 means accepted, not sent: poll the status.\n\nOn the registry-test environment the gateway is a fake 8028: nothing reaches a real phone."
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// A fresh Idempotency-Key, source_reference and expires_at per request. Requests with the",
          "// X-Keep-Key header reuse the previous request's values (replay and conflict checks).",
          "if (!pm.request.headers.has('X-Keep-Key')) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('idempotencyKey', 'pm-' + pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sourceReference', 'postman:' + Date.now());",
          "  // expires_at: 5 minutes ahead for OTPs, 30 minutes for everything else.",
          "  const ttl = (pm.request.name || '').toLowerCase().includes('otp') ? 5 : 30;",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('expiresAt', new Date(Date.now() + ttl * 60000).toISOString().replace(/\\.\\d{3}Z$/, 'Z'));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "idempotencyKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "sourceReference",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "expiresAt",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "messageId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "lastKey",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Process is up. No token.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/livez",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "livez"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Database reachable and the service ready for traffic. No token.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/readyz",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "readyz"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Send SMS",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 202 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('messageId', b.id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('lastKey', b.idempotency_key);",
                  "  pm.test('response never carries the text', () => pm.expect(b).to.not.have.property('text'));",
                  "  pm.test('status is accepted', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('accepted'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{callerToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{idempotencyKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "description": "An OTP: `expires_at` required (the code's own expiry), one SMS part, highest priority. OAN never sends it after `expires_at`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"recipient\": \"{{recipient}}\",\n  \"text\": \"Your OAN code is 123456. It expires in 5 minutes. Do not share it.\",\n  \"purpose\": \"otp\",\n  \"source_reference\": \"{{sourceReference}}\",\n  \"expires_at\": \"{{expiresAt}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages/sms",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "messages",
                "sms"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Message status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('recipient is masked', () => pm.expect(s.recipient_masked).to.include('*'));",
                  "pm.test('no text in the status', () => pm.expect(s).to.not.have.property('text'));",
                  "console.log('status', s.status, 'final', s.final, 'provider', s.provider_status || '-');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{callerToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Status of a message this caller submitted. Never contains the text; the recipient is masked. Statuses: accepted, sending, sent, delivered (final), expired, failed, unknown (final). Never resubmit an `unknown` message under a new key: 8028 may have sent it.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages/{{messageId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "messages",
                "{{messageId}}"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
